   "text": {
    "L1": "A pictograph uses pictures to show data. First, read the key.",
    "L2": "The key says one tree picture stands for 10 trees.",
    "L3": "Some people count a half picture as one whole picture. That is not correct.",
    "L4": "Three full pictures stand for 3 times 10, or 30 trees.",
    "L5": "A half picture stands for half of 10, which is 5 trees.",
    "L6": "Add the full-picture value and the half-picture value. The total is 35 trees.",
    "L7": "The key must stay the same when you read every picture in the row.",
    "L8": "Now choose the total for this pictograph."
   },
